      "value": "# Construction Glossary\nQuick reference for industry acronyms, abbreviations, and terminology.\n\n---\n\n## Project Delivery & Contracts\n\n| Term | Definition |\n|------|------------|\n| **DB** | Design-Build — Single entity provides design and construction |\n| **DBB** | Design-Bid-Build — Traditional delivery, separate design and construction contracts |\n| **CMAR** | Construction Manager at Risk — CM guarantees price, provides precon services |\n| **CM Agency** | Construction Manager as Agent — CM advises owner, no financial risk |\n| **IPD** | Integrated Project Delivery — Collaborative, shared risk/reward model |\n| **GMP** | Guaranteed Maximum Price — Contractor's price ceiling |\n| **Lump Sum** | Fixed price contract for defined scope |\n| **Cost-Plus** | Contractor paid actual costs plus fee |\n| **T&M** | Time and Materials — Payment based on hours and materials used |\n| **NTP** | Notice to Proceed — Official authorization to start work |\n| **LOI** | Letter of Intent — Preliminary agreement before formal contract |\n| **LOA** | Letter of Award — Notification of successful bid |\n\n---\n\n## Project Phases & Milestones\n\n| Term | Definition |\n|------|------------|\n| **Precon** | Preconstruction — Planning, estimating, scheduling before construction |\n| **Mobilization** | Setting up site, equipment, personnel before work begins |\n| **Substantial Completion** | Project is sufficiently complete for intended use |\n| **Punch List** | List of items to complete/correct before final acceptance |\n| **Final Completion** | All work complete, all closeout documents submitted |\n| **CO** | Certificate of Occupancy — Building official's approval to occupy |\n| **Turnover** | Transfer of project from contractor to owner |\n| **Closeout** | Final phase: as-builts, warranties, O&Ms, final payment |\n\n---\n\n## Documentation Types\n\n| Term | Definition |\n|------|------------|\n| **RFI** | Request for Information — Question to clarify design/documents |\n| **RFI Log** | Tracking document for all RFIs and their status |\n| **Submittal** | Documents/samples submitted for approval before fabrication/installation |\n| **Shop Drawing** | Detailed fabrication/installation drawings by subcontractor/supplier |\n| **Product Data** | Manufacturer's specs, performance data, installation instructions |\n| **CO** | Change Order — Formal modification to contract (price, time, scope) |\n| **PCO** | Proposed Change Order — Change order request before approval |\n| **ASR** | Architect's Supplemental Instructions — Minor changes without cost impact |\n| **CCD** | Construction Change Directive — Owner-directed change before price agreement |\n| **P&M** | Pay Application (or AIA G702/G703) — Monthly payment request |\n| **Lien Waiver** | Document waiving right to file mechanics lien upon payment |\n| **Schedule of Values** | Breakdown of contract price for progress payments |\n| **As-Builts** | Drawings marked up to show actual installed conditions |\n| **O&M** | Operations and Maintenance Manual — Equipment documentation for owner |\n\n---\n\n## Drawing & Specification Terms\n\n| Term | Definition |\n|------|------------|\n| **CDs** | Construction Documents — Final design documents for construction |\n| **DD** | Design Development — Intermediate design phase |\n| **SD** | Schematic Design — Early design phase |\n| **Specs** | Specifications — Written technical requirements |\n| **CSI** | Construction Specifications Institute — Organization that developed MasterFormat |\n| **MasterFormat** | Standard numbering system for specs (e.g., 03 30 00 Cast-in-Place Concrete) |\n| **UniFormat** | Preliminary project description system (Level 1-5) |\n| **Sheet Index** | List of all drawings in a set |\n| **Legend** | Symbols and abbreviations used on drawings |\n| **Detail** | Large-scale drawing showing specific construction |\n| **Section** | Drawing showing cut-through view |\n| **Elevation** | Drawing showing vertical face/exterior |\n| **Plan** | Drawing showing view from above |\n| **Keynote** | Numbered reference on drawings to spec or note |\n| **Reference Drawing** | Drawing referred to for additional information |\n\n---\n\n## Organizations & Standards\n\n| Term | Definition |\n|------|------------|\n| **AIA** | American Institute of Architects — Publishes standard contract forms |\n| **AGC** | Associated General Contractors of America |\n| **ABC** | Associated Builders and Contractors |\n| **OSHA** | Occupational Safety and Health Administration |\n| **ICC** | International Code Council — Publishes IBC, IRC, etc. |\n| **IBC** | International Building Code |\n| **IRC** | International Residential Code |\n| **NFPA** | National Fire Protection Association — Fire and life safety codes |\n| **ASTM** | ASTM International — Material and testing standards |\n| **ANSI** | American National Standards Institute |\n| **ASCE** | American Society of Civil Engineers |\n| **ASME** | American Society of Mechanical Engineers |\n| **IEEE** | Institute of Electrical and Electronics Engineers |\n| **UL** | Underwriters Laboratories — Product safety certification |\n| **FM** | Factory Mutual — Insurance-related testing and standards |\n\n---\n\n## Roles & Stakeholders\n\n| Term | Definition |\n|------|------------|\n| **Owner** | Project owner/developer who funds and owns the project |\n| **GC** | General Contractor — Prime contractor managing construction |\n| **CM** | Construction Manager — Manages project (varies by delivery method) |\n| **Sub** | Subcontractor — Specialty contractor under GC |\n| **Prime** | Prime contractor — Contractor with direct contract to owner |\n| **A/E** | Architect/Engineer — Design professionals |\n| **PM** | Project Manager — Manages project for GC or owner |\n| **PE** | Project Engineer — Supports PM with documentation, coordination |\n| **Super** | Superintendent — On-site field supervisor |\n| **Foreman** | Crew supervisor for specific trade/work area |\n| **Inspector** | Building official or special inspector verifying compliance |\n| **Special Inspector** | Third-party inspector for structural, fire, etc. per IBC |\n| **Testing Agency** | Third-party materials testing lab |\n| **Surety** | Bonding company providing performance/payment bonds |\n\n---\n\n## Bidding & Procurement\n\n| Term | Definition |\n|------|------------|\n| **IFB** | Invitation to Bid — Formal solicitation for bids |\n| **RFP** | Request for Proposal — Solicitation often including qualifications |\n| **RFQ** | Request for Qualifications — Solicitation based on qualifications |\n| **Bid Tab** | Bid tabulation — Summary comparing all bids received |\n| **Base Bid** | Primary bid amount for basic scope |\n| **Alternate** | Additive or deductive option to base bid |\n| **Allowance** | Budget amount for undefined work or materials |\n| **Unit Price** | Price per unit for estimated quantities (e.g., CY, LF) |\n| **Bid Bond** | Guarantee bidder will enter contract if selected |\n| **Performance Bond** | Surety guarantee of contractor performance |\n| **Payment Bond** | Surety guarantee that subcontractors/suppliers will be paid |\n| **Pre-Bid Meeting** | Meeting for prospective bidders before bid date |\n| **Prequalification** | Process to vet contractors before allowing them to bid |\n| **Scope Gap** | Missing scope in bid — risk of claims |\n\n---\n\n## Safety Terms\n\n| Term | Definition |\n|------|------------|\n| **JHA/JSA** | Job Hazard/Safety Analysis — Task-specific hazard assessment |\n| **PPE** | Personal Protective Equipment |\n| **SDS** | Safety Data Sheet — Formerly MSDS, chemical hazard info |\n| **GFCI** | Ground Fault Circuit Interrupter — Electrical protection |\n| **LOTO** | Lockout/Tagout — Energy isolation procedure |\n| **Confined Space** | Space with limited entry/exit, potential hazards |\n| **Trenching** | Excavation deeper than it is wide |\n| **Competent Person** | OSHA-defined role for excavation, scaffolding, etc. |\n| **OSHA 300 Log** | Record of work-related injuries/illnesses |\n| **EMR** | Experience Modification Rate — Workers comp rating |\n| **TRIR** | Total Recordable Incident Rate |\n| **DART** | Days Away, Restricted, or Transferred rate |\n| **Near Miss** | Incident that could have caused injury but didn't |\n| **Toolbox Talk** | Short safety meeting at start of shift |\n\n---\n\n## Scheduling Terms\n\n| Term | Definition |\n|------|------------|\n| **CPM** | Critical Path Method — Schedule analysis technique |\n| **Critical Path** | Longest path through schedule; determines project duration |\n| **Float** | Slack — Time an activity can be delayed without affecting completion |\n| **Free Float** | Time activity can be delayed without delaying successors |\n| **Total Float** | Time activity can be delayed without delaying project completion |\n| **Milestone** | Key date with zero duration (e.g., Substantial Completion) |\n| **LAG** | Delay between predecessor and successor |\n| **Predecessor** | Activity that must complete before another can start |\n| **Successor** | Activity that depends on another activity |\n| **TIA** | Time Impact Analysis — Method to quantify delay impact |\n| **Fringe** | Time between activity and crew availability |\n| **Resource Loading** | Assigning resources (labor, equipment) to activities |\n| **Lookahead** | Rolling schedule review (typically 2-6 weeks) |\n\n---\n\n## Financial Terms\n\n| Term | Definition |\n|------|------------|\n| **Retainage** | Percentage held back from payments until completion |\n| **Bonding Capacity** | Maximum project size surety will bond |\n| **Working Capital** | Funds available for day-to-day operations |\n| **Cash Flow** | Movement of money in/out of project |\n| **Underbilling** | Work performed exceeds amount billed |\n| **Overbilling** | Amount billed exceeds work performed (front-loading) |\n| **Backcharge** | Deduction from subcontractor for work performed by others |\n| **Unit Cost** | Cost per measured unit |\n| **Direct Cost** | Labor, materials, equipment directly for work |\n| **Indirect Cost** | Overhead, supervision, insurance, bonds |\n| **Fee** | Contractor's profit and home office overhead |\n| **Escalation** | Cost increase over time due to inflation |\n| **Contingency** | Budget for unknown conditions/changes |\n| **General Conditions** | Project-specific overhead (supervision, trailers, etc.) |\n\n---\n\n## Measurements & Quantities\n\n| Abbreviation | Meaning |\n|--------------|---------|\n| **SF** | Square Feet |\n| **SY** | Square Yards |\n| **CF** | Cubic Feet |\n| **CY** | Cubic Yards |\n| **LF** | Linear Feet |\n| **LS** | Lump Sum |\n| **EA** | Each |\n| **Tons** | 2,000 lbs (or metric tonne = 2,204.6 lbs) |\n| **MBF** | Thousand Board Feet (lumber) |\n| **Kips** | Thousand pounds (structural) |\n| **PSF** | Pounds per Square Foot |\n| **PSI** | Pounds per Square Inch |\n| **GPM** | Gallons Per Minute |\n| **CFM** | Cubic Feet per Minute |\n| **KW** | Kilowatts |\n| **KVA** | Kilovolt-Amperes |\n| **Amps** | Amperes |\n| **V** | Volts |\n\n---\n\n## Common Abbreviations on Drawings\n\n| Abbreviation | Meaning |\n|--------------|---------|\n| **TYP** | Typical |\n| **SIM** | Similar |\n| **OC** | On Center |\n| **E.W.P.** | Each Way, Perpendicular |\n| **E.F.** | Each Face |\n| **T&B** | Top and Bottom |\n| **REF** | Reference |\n| **NIC** | Not In Contract |\n| **N.T.S.** | Not To Scale |\n| **EX** | Existing |\n| **PROP** | Proposed |\n| **DEM** | Demolish |\n| **RELOC** | Relocate |\n| **ALT** | Alternate |\n| **BLDG** | Building |\n| **FL** | Floor |\n| **CL** | Centerline |\n| **EL** | Elevation |\n| **FFL** | Finished Floor Level |\n| **TOS** | Top of Steel |\n| **BOS** | Bottom of Steel |\n| **INV** | Invert (pipe elevation) |\n| **HT** | Height |\n| **WD** | Width |\n| **DP** | Depth |\n\n---\n\n## Quick Reference: Most Common Acronyms\n\n| Acronym | Meaning | Context |\n|---------|---------|---------|\n| **RFI** | Request for Information | Documentation |\n| **CO** | Change Order | Documentation |\n| **NTP** | Notice to Proceed | Contracts |\n| **GMP** | Guaranteed Maximum Price | Contracts |\n| **Substantial** | Substantial Completion | Milestone |\n| **Punch List** | Items to complete | Closeout |\n| **As-Builts** | Record drawings | Closeout |\n| **O&M** | Operations & Maintenance | Closeout |\n| **OSHA** | Safety administration | Safety |\n| **PPE** | Personal protective equipment | Safety |\n| **CPM** | Critical Path Method | Scheduling |\n| **Float** | Schedule flexibility | Scheduling |\n| **GC** | General Contractor | Roles |\n| **Sub** | Subcontractor | Roles |\n| **A/E** | Architect/Engineer | Roles |\n\n---\n\n## Adding to This Glossary\n\nWhen you encounter new acronyms or terms, I can add them to this reference. Just say:\n- *\"Add [TERM] to the glossary\"*\n- *\"What does [ACRONYM] mean?\"*\n\nThis glossary grows with your project needs.",
