      "value": "# Construction Templates\nIndustry-specific prompt templates optimized for construction documentation and workflows.\n\n---\n\n## RFI (Request for Information) Templates\n\n### RFI Draft Request\n```\nROLE: Act as an experienced construction project manager\nTASK: Draft an RFI based on the following situation\nCONTEXT: \n- Project: [Project name/type]\n- Issue: [Description of conflict, discrepancy, or clarification needed]\n- Impact: [Schedule/cost implications if unresolved]\n- Specs reference: [Relevant specification sections]\nCONSTRAINTS: \n- Use professional, concise language\n- Reference specific drawing/spec sections\n- Include photos/sketches reference if applicable\nOUTPUT: Professional RFI document with: RFI #, Date, Subject, Reference Documents, Question, Suggested Response (if any), Impact Statement\n```\n\n### RFI Response Analysis\n```\nROLE: Construction contract administrator\nTASK: Analyze this RFI response for completeness and contract implications\nCONTEXT: [Original RFI context and received response]\nCONSTRAINTS: Consider contractual obligations, schedule impacts, and cost implications\nOUTPUT: \n1. Response Adequacy Assessment (1-10)\n2. Clarifying Questions (if needed)\n3. Contract/Legal Implications\n4. Next Steps\n```\n\n---\n\n## Submittal Templates\n\n### Submittal Review Prompt\n```\nROLE: Quality control manager for a general contractor\nTASK: Review this submittal for compliance with project specifications\nCONTEXT:\n- Submittal type: [Product data / Shop drawing / Sample / etc.]\n- Spec section: [Reference]\n- Project phase: [Phase]\nCONSTRAINTS:\n- Check against specified requirements\n- Note any deviations\n- Verify coordination with other trades\nOUTPUT: Structured review with:\n1. Compliance Status (Approved/Approved as Noted/Revise & Resubmit/Rejected)\n2. Deviations from Specs\n3. Coordination Items\n4. Action Items for Subcontractor\n```\n\n---\n\n## Change Order Templates\n\n### Change Order Request Draft\n```\nROLE: Senior project manager preparing change order documentation\nTASK: Draft a formal change order request\nCONTEXT:\n- Project: [Details]\n- Change description: [What changed and why]\n- Cause: [Owner request / Unforeseen condition / Design error / etc.]\n- Schedule impact: [Days]\n- Cost impact: [Breakdown]\nCONSTRAINTS:\n- Reference contract clause\n- Justify entitlement\n- Provide detailed cost breakdown\nOUTPUT: Complete change order document with backup documentation\n```\n\n### Change Order Negotiation Prompt\n```\nROLE: Construction contract negotiator\nTASK: Analyze this change order and provide negotiation strategy\nCONTEXT: [Change order details and context]\nCONSTRAINTS:\n- Consider fair market pricing\n- Reference RSMeans or historical data\n- Identify areas for negotiation\nOUTPUT:\n1. Pricing Analysis (reasonable/inflated/underpriced)\n2. Negotiation Strategy\n3. Counter-offer Recommendations\n4. Talking Points\n```\n\n---\n\n## Bidding Templates\n\n### Bid Analysis Prompt\n```\nROLE: Chief estimator evaluating competitive bids\nTASK: Analyze and compare these bids for a construction project\nCONTEXT:\n- Project: [Scope, size, type]\n- Bid list: [Number of bidders]\n- Lowest bid: [Amount]\n- Next lowest: [Amount]\nCONSTRAINTS:\n- Check for scope gaps\n- Identify unbalanced bidding\n- Verify contractor qualifications\nOUTPUT:\n1. Bid Tabulation\n2. Scope Compliance Check\n3. Risk Assessment per Bidder\n4. Recommendation with Justification\n```\n\n### Subcontractor Prequalification Prompt\n```\nROLE: Prequalification specialist for a GC\nTASK: Evaluate this subcontractor for project prequalification\nCONTEXT:\n- Subcontractor: [Company info]\n- Project: [Upcoming project details]\n- Requirements: [Bonding capacity, safety rating, relevant experience]\nOUTPUT:\n1. Financial Assessment\n2. Safety Performance Evaluation\n3. Relevant Experience Matrix\n4. Capacity Analysis\n5. Recommendation (Approved/Conditional/Not Approved)\n```\n\n---\n\n## Safety Document Templates\n\n### Job Hazard Analysis Prompt\n```\nROLE: Site safety manager\nTASK: Create a comprehensive Job Hazard Analysis (JHA) for this construction activity\nCONTEXT:\n- Activity: [Specific work task]\n- Location: [Site conditions]\n- Crew size: [Number of workers]\nCONSTRAINTS:\n- Follow OSHA requirements\n- Include specific PPE requirements\n- Address site-specific hazards\nOUTPUT: Formal JHA with:\n1. Task Steps\n2. Potential Hazards per Step\n3. Control Measures\n4. Required PPE\n5. Training Requirements\n```\n\n### Incident Investigation Prompt\n```\nROLE: Safety director conducting incident investigation\nTASK: Analyze this incident and develop corrective actions\nCONTEXT:\n- Incident: [Description of what occurred]\n- Injuries/damage: [Details]\n- Witnesses: [Statements]\nCONSTRAINTS:\n- Root cause analysis required\n- Reference OSHA standards\n- Prevent recurrence focus\nOUTPUT:\n1. Incident Summary\n2. Root Cause Analysis (5 Whys)\n3. Contributing Factors\n4. Corrective Actions\n5. Preventive Measures\n6. Training Recommendations\n```\n\n---\n\n## Schedule Templates\n\n### Schedule Impact Analysis Prompt\n```\nROLE: Scheduler with Primavera P6 expertise\nTASK: Analyze this schedule delay and prepare time impact analysis\nCONTEXT:\n- Project: [Details, original duration]\n- Delay event: [Description and dates]\n- Critical path: [Status]\n- Float available: [Days]\nCONSTRAINTS:\n- Use AACE best practices\n- Consider concurrent delays\n- Reference contract requirements\nOUTPUT: Time Impact Analysis (TIA) with:\n1. Event Description\n2. Affected Activities\n3. Critical Path Impact\n4. Float Consumption\n5. Extension Entitlement\n6. Recovery Options\n```\n\n---\n\n## Correspondence Templates\n\n### Professional Letter Draft\n```\nROLE: Construction contract administrator\nTASK: Draft a professional letter regarding [topic]\nCONTEXT:\n- Recipient: [Name, title, company]\n- Purpose: [Communication objective]\n- Background: [Relevant project history]\n- Tone: [Formal / Semi-formal / Direct]\nCONSTRAINTS:\n- Professional construction industry standards\n- Clear and actionable\n- Reference contract documents as needed\nOUTPUT: Complete letter with proper formatting\n```\n\n### Meeting Minutes Prompt\n```\nROLE: Project engineer documenting project meeting\nTASK: Generate professional meeting minutes\nCONTEXT:\n- Meeting type: [Owner-Architect-Contractor / Subcontractor / Safety / etc.]\n- Attendees: [List]\n- Topics discussed: [Summary]\nCONSTRAINTS:\n- Capture action items with responsible parties and due dates\n- Document decisions made\n- Note open issues\nOUTPUT: Structured meeting minutes with:\n1. Meeting Information\n2. Attendees\n3. Agenda Items\n4. Discussion Summary\n5. Action Items Table\n6. Next Meeting\n```\n\n---\n\n## Prompt Optimization Tips by Document Type\n\n### For RFIs:\n- Always include specific drawing/spec references\n- State impact clearly (cost/schedule)\n- Suggest solution if you have one\n- Keep it factual, not accusatory\n\n### For Submittals:\n- Reference specific spec sections\n- Note coordination requirements\n- Include approval timeline needs\n\n### For Change Orders:\n- Establish entitlement first\n- Provide detailed cost breakdown\n- Document schedule impact\n- Reference contract clauses\n\n### For Bidding:\n- Define scope clearly\n- List all exclusions\n- Specify bid format requirements\n- Include qualification criteria",
