      "value": "# Prompt Engineering Frameworks\nComprehensive guide to all prompt engineering frameworks for crafting effective prompts.\n\n---\n\n## OVERVIEW\n\n| Framework | Best For | Complexity |\n|-----------|----------|------------|\n| **CTF** | Teaching beginners, simple prompts | ⭐ Easy |\n| **RTCCO** | Comprehensive prompts, internal use | ⭐⭐ Medium |\n| **RASCEF** | Action-oriented prompts | ⭐⭐ Medium |\n| **PRIME** | Structured requirements | ⭐⭐ Medium |\n| **5C** | Iterative refinement | ⭐⭐⭐ Advanced |\n| **4-Layer** | Robust, failure-resistant prompts | ⭐⭐⭐ Advanced |\n| **P.R.O.M.P.T** | Complete planning framework | ⭐⭐⭐ Advanced |\n\n---\n\n## 1. CTF Framework (Context, Task, Format)\n**Best for:** Teaching beginners, quick prompts, construction documents\n\n### Structure\nCONTEXT: [Background info, project details, stakeholder context]\nTASK: [Specific action you want the AI to perform]\nFORMAT: [How you want the output structured]\n\n### When to Use\n- Quick prompt construction\n- Teaching prompt engineering basics\n- Simple, single-purpose requests\n- Construction documentation (RFIs, submittals, emails)\n\n---\n\n## 2. RTCCO Framework (Role, Task, Context, Constraints, Output)\n**Best for:** Comprehensive prompts, professional documents, internal use\n\n### Structure\nROLE: [Who the AI should act as]\nTASK: [Specific action to perform]\nCONTEXT: [Background, project details, stakeholder info]\nCONSTRAINTS: [Limitations, requirements, must-haves/must-nots]\nOUTPUT: [Format, length, structure requirements]\n\n### When to Use\n- Internal prompt building (use CTF for teaching)\n- Complex, multi-part requests\n- Professional document generation\n\n---\n\n## 3. RASCEF Framework (Role, Action, Steps, Context, Examples, Format)\n**Best for:** Action-oriented prompts, step-by-step processes\n\n### When to Use\n- Step-by-step processes\n- Safety plans, procedures\n- When you need specific actions enumerated\n\n---\n\n## 4. PRIME Framework (Purpose, Requirements, Instructions, Metrics, Examples)\n**Best for:** Structured requirements, project specifications\n\n### When to Use\n- Bid proposals\n- Project specifications\n- When you have specific requirements to meet\n\n---\n\n## 5. 5C Framework (Clarity, Contextualization, Command, Chaining, Continuous Refinement)\n**Best for:** Iterative improvement, complex workflows\n\n### Components\n1. Clarity: Be specific and unambiguous\n2. Contextualization: Provide relevant background\n3. Command: Give clear instructions\n4. Chaining: Break into sequential steps\n5. Continuous Refinement: Iterate and improve\n\n---\n\n## 6. 4-Layer Framework (Core Instruction, Context Independence, Model-Agnostic Language, Failure-Resistant Design)\n**Best for:** Robust prompts, cross-platform compatibility\n\n### When to Use\n- Cross-platform prompts\n- Critical documents where failure is costly\n- Enterprise applications\n\n---\n\n## 7. P.R.O.M.P.T. Framework (Purpose, Results Format, Obstacles, Mindset, Preferences, Technical)\n**Best for:** Complete planning, comprehensive specifications\n\n### When to Use\n- Complete planning documents\n- Safety briefings, training materials\n- Complex projects with many requirements\n\n---\n\n## FRAMEWORK SELECTION GUIDE\n\n| Your Goal | Use This Framework |\n|-----------|-------------------|\n| Quick, simple prompt | CTF |\n| Teaching prompt engineering | CTF |\n| Comprehensive document | RTCCO |\n| Step-by-step process | RASCEF |\n| Bid/proposal with requirements | PRIME |\n| Iterative refinement | 5C |\n| Cross-platform compatibility | 4-Layer |\n| Complete planning | P.R.O.M.P.T |\n| Construction document (RFI, submittal) | CTF or RTCCO |\n| Safety documentation | RASCEF or P.R.O.M.P.T |\n\n---\n\n## TEACHING APPROACH\n\nWhen teaching prompt engineering to construction professionals:\n\n1. Start with CTF - Simple, memorable, effective for 80% of use cases\n2. Introduce RTCCO for complex needs\n3. Reference others as advanced options when specific needs arise\n\nThe goal is accessibility, not overwhelm. Most users will be well-served by CTF alone.",
      "limit": 100000,
      "project_id": null,
      "template_name": null,
