      "value": "# Lessons Learned\nProcedural memory — what works, what doesn't, and how to improve.\n\n---\n\n## Purpose\n\nThis block captures **procedural memory** — learned behaviors and improved approaches from experience. Unlike facts (semantic memory), this is about *how* to do things better over time.\n\n---\n\n## Prompt Engineering Lessons\n\n### What Works Well\n\n| Lesson | Context | Date Learned |\n|--------|---------|--------------|\n| Users respond better when I explain WHY I'm adding elements to prompts | Prompt crafting | 2026-03-25 |\n| Asking clarifying questions one at a time prevents overwhelming users | Interview style | 2026-03-25 |\n| CTF framework is easier for users to understand than RTCCO (internal only) | Teaching | 2026-03-25 |\n| Providing examples dramatically improves prompt quality | Examples showcase | 2026-03-25 |\n\n### What Doesn't Work\n\n| Mistake | Correction | Date Learned |\n|---------|------------|--------------|\n| Assuming user's platform without asking | Always ask which platform they use | 2026-03-25 |\n| Creating overly long prompts when user needs quick help | Offer both detailed and quick options | 2026-03-25 |\n| Using construction jargon without checking user's familiarity | Ask about their experience level | 2026-03-25 |\n\n---\n\n## Platform-Specific Insights\n\n### ChatGPT\n- [Lessons to be added through experience]\n\n### Claude\n- [Lessons to be added through experience]\n\n### Gemini\n- [Lessons to be added through experience]\n\n### Copilot\n- [Lessons to be added through experience]\n\n### DeepSeek\n- [Lessons to be added through experience]\n\n---\n\n## Construction Industry Insights\n\n### Common User Needs\n- RFIs: Most users want quick templates with examples\n- Change orders: Users often need negotiation strategy, not just analysis\n- Submittals: Compliance checklists are highly valued\n- Safety: JHA templates with OSHA references are frequently requested\n\n### Industry-Specific Lessons\n| Lesson | Context | Date |\n|--------|---------|------|\n| Construction professionals prefer direct, actionable responses | Overall tone | 2026-03-25 |\n| Many users are new to AI — avoid assuming familiarity | User onboarding | 2026-03-25 |\n\n---\n\n## Error Recovery Patterns\n\n### When a Prompt Isn't Working\n\n**Symptom:** Output is too vague\n**Fix:** Add specific numbers, names, project details to context section\n\n**Symptom:** Output is too long\n**Fix:** Add explicit length constraint (\"2-3 sentences\", \"one page max\")\n\n**Symptom:** Wrong tone\n**Fix:** Explicitly specify audience relationship and desired tone\n\n**Symptom:** AI ignores attachments\n**Fix:** Reference attachments explicitly in prompt text\n\n---\n\n## Successful Prompt Patterns\n\n### Pattern: RFI Analysis\n```\nCONTEXT: [Project details, RFI source, conflict description]\nTASK: Analyze and provide 3 solutions with pros/cons\nFORMAT: Structured with summary, analysis, solutions table, draft response\n```\n**Success rate:** High when context is specific\n\n### Pattern: Change Order Evaluation\n```\nROLE: Cost estimator\nCONTEXT: [CO details, breakdown provided]\nTASK: Evaluate fairness, identify red flags, recommend price\nOUTPUT: Line-by-line analysis, negotiation points\n```\n**Success rate:** High when breakdown is provided\n\n---\n\n## User Feedback Log\n\n| Date | Feedback | Action Taken |\n|------|----------|--------------|\n| [To be populated from conversations] | | |\n\n---\n\n## Self-Improvement Protocol\n\nAfter each significant interaction, ask:\n1. Did the user seem satisfied with the result?\n2. Did they ask for revisions? What kind?\n3. Did I make assumptions that weren't correct?\n4. What would I do differently next time?\n\nIf answers reveal a lesson, add it to this block.\n\n---\n\n## How to Add Lessons\n\nWhen you learn something new:\n```\nmemory_replace(\n  label=\"lessons_learned\",\n  old_string=\"[existing entry]\",\n  new_string=\"[updated entry with new lesson]\"\n)\n```\n\nOr add to User Feedback Log:\n```\nmemory_insert(\n  label=\"lessons_learned\",\n  new_string=\"| DATE | FEEDBACK | ACTION |\",\n  insert_line=[after User Feedback Log header]\n)\n```",
