    {
      "value": "# Migration Templates\nStep-by-step guides for migrating context, prompts, and preferences between AI platforms.\n\n---\n\n## Migration Overview\n\n### Why Migrate Between Platforms?\n- **Feature differences**: Claude excels at long documents, ChatGPT has plugins, Copilot integrates with Microsoft 365\n- **Cost considerations**: Different pricing models for teams vs. individuals\n- **Security requirements**: Enterprise needs may favor specific platforms\n- **Task specialization**: Some platforms better for certain tasks (coding, analysis, creative)\n\n### Migration Principles:\n1. **Preserve context** - User role, project details, preferences\n2. **Adapt format** - Each platform has different instruction structures\n3. **Test thoroughly** - Verify migrated prompts work as expected\n4. **Iterate** - Refine based on results\n\n---\n\n## ChatGPT → Claude Migration\n\n### Step 1: Export ChatGPT Custom Instructions\n**From ChatGPT:**\n1. Go to Settings → Personalization → Custom Instructions\n2. Copy both sections:\n   - \"What would you like ChatGPT to know about you?\"\n   - \"How would you like ChatGPT to respond?\"\n\n### Step 2: Adapt for Claude\n**Claude Structure:**\n- Claude uses **System Prompt** (one comprehensive block)\n- Claude Projects allows **Knowledge Files** for extended context\n\n### Step 3: Migration Template\n```\nCombine ChatGPT's two sections into Claude's single system prompt:\n\n[FROM: What would you like ChatGPT to know about you?]\nI am a [ROLE] in the construction industry, specializing in [AREAS]. \nI typically work on [PROJECT TYPES] ranging from [SIZE/VALUE].\nMy responsibilities include [KEY TASKS].\n\n[FROM: How would you like ChatGPT to respond? - Adapted for Claude]\nWhen assisting me:\n- Communication style: [preferences]\n- Document formatting: [preferences]\n- Analysis approach: [preferences]\n\nADDITIONAL CLAUDE-SPECIFIC ELEMENTS:\n- For complex analysis, use extended thinking to show your reasoning\n- When documents are attached, reference specific sections\n- Provide multiple options when decisions are needed\n- Flag when information is insufficient\n```\n\n### Step 4: Use Claude Projects for Extended Context\nUpload as Knowledge File:\n- Project specifications summary\n- Company templates\n- Relevant codes/standards excerpts\n- Past correspondence examples\n\n### Step 5: Test Key Use Cases\n1. Draft a sample RFI\n2. Analyze a change order\n3. Create a meeting summary\n4. Compare results to ChatGPT output\n\n### Step 6: Refine\n- Note any differences in response style\n- Adjust instructions for Claude's tendencies\n- Add platform-specific preferences\n\n---\n\n## Claude → ChatGPT Migration\n\n### Step 1: Document Claude Setup\n**From Claude:**\n1. Copy System Prompt content\n2. Download any Knowledge Files\n3. Note successful prompt patterns\n\n### Step 2: Split for ChatGPT's Two-Section Format\n**Section 1: \"What would you like ChatGPT to know about you?\"**\n```\nExtract user context from Claude setup:\n- Professional role and industry\n- Project types and typical scope\n- Primary responsibilities\n- Stakeholders you work with\n- Construction-specific knowledge areas\n```\n\n**Section 2: \"How would you like ChatGPT to respond?\"**\n```\nExtract behavioral instructions:\n- Communication style preferences\n- Document formatting requirements\n- Analysis approach\n- Tone and formality level\n- Constraint and limitations\n```\n\n### Step 3: Migration Template\n**Section 1 (About You):**\n```\nI work in construction as a [ROLE from Claude system prompt].\nMy focus is [PROJECT TYPES] in [REGION/MARKET].\nI manage [SIZE/RANGE] projects involving [KEY ACTIVITIES].\nI regularly interact with [STAKEHOLDERS].\nCurrent project: [IF APPLICABLE]\n```\n\n**Section 2 (Response Preferences):**\n```\nCommunication:\n- [Tone preferences from Claude]\n- [Formatting preferences]\n- [Level of detail expected]\n\nDocuments:\n- [Document types you create]\n- [Templates to reference]\n- [Industry standards to cite]\n\nAnalysis:\n- [How you want options presented]\n- [Risk tolerance for suggestions]\n- [When to ask clarifying questions]\n\nConstraints:\n- [Topics requiring professional review]\n- [Assumptions to avoid]\n- [Information to never fabricate]\n```\n\n### Step 4: Use ChatGPT Memory\n- ChatGPT can remember across conversations\n- Enable Memory in Settings\n- Key facts persist automatically\n\n### Step 5: Consider Creating a Custom GPT\nFor specialized tasks, create a GPT:\n- Upload knowledge files (from Claude Projects)\n- Define specific behaviors\n- Share with team members\n\n---\n\n## ChatGPT/Claude → Gemini Migration\n\n### Step 1: Gather Source Content\n- Custom instructions (ChatGPT) or System prompt (Claude)\n- Knowledge files/context\n- Successful prompt templates\n\n### Step 2: Adapt to Gemini's Format\nGemini uses **System Instructions** (single block)\n\n### Step 3: Migration Template\n```\n# Gemini System Instructions\n\n## User Context\n[User role, industry, project types from source]\n\n## Primary Tasks\n[List of typical tasks user needs help with]\n\n## Response Guidelines\n[Behavioral preferences adapted from source]\n\n## Knowledge Areas\n[Construction expertise areas]\n\n## Output Formats\n[Document templates and formatting preferences]\n\n## Constraints\n[Limitations and professional review requirements]\n\n## Gemini-Specific Features\n- Use long context window for document analysis\n- Reference uploaded files directly\n- Leverage Google Search for current code/standard verification\n```\n\n### Step 4: Upload Context Files\nGemini accepts file uploads:\n- PDF specs\n- Project documents\n- Reference materials\n\n### Step 5: Test Migration\nCompare Gemini output to source platform for:\n- Document quality\n- Analysis depth\n- Instruction adherence\n\n---\n\n## Any Platform → Microsoft Copilot Migration\n\n### Step 1: Extract Core Elements\nFrom source platform:\n- User role and context\n- Task descriptions\n- Communication preferences\n- Document templates\n\n### Step 2: Leverage Copilot's Strengths\nCopilot is optimized for:\n- Microsoft 365 integration (Word, Excel, PowerPoint, Outlook)\n- Enterprise data access\n- Web search capability\n\n### Step 3: Migration Template\n```\n# Copilot Context for Construction Professional\n\n## About Me\nI'm a [ROLE] in construction, managing [PROJECT TYPES].\nMy work involves [KEY RESPONSIBILITIES].\n\n## How I Use Copilot\nPrimary tasks:\n- [Task 1 with Microsoft app context: e.g., \"Draft RFIs in Word\"]\n- [Task 2: e.g., \"Analyze change orders in Excel\"]\n- [Task 3: e.g., \"Create project presentations in PowerPoint\"]\n\n## Document Standards\nWhen I ask for documents:\n- Format for [Word/Excel/PowerPoint as appropriate]\n- Use my company templates (describe or reference)\n- Include professional formatting\n\n## Communication Style\n[Preferences from source platform]\n\n## Microsoft 365 Integration\n- Reference documents I share\n- Maintain formatting when creating files\n- Use Excel formulas and formatting appropriately\n- Create Outlook-ready emails when requested\n\n## Professional Constraints\n[Standard construction industry constraints]\n```\n\n### Step 4: Enterprise Considerations\n- Copilot respects enterprise data boundaries\n- No external training on company data\n- Can access organizational context\n\n---\n\n## Migration Decision Matrix\n\n### Choose Your Migration Path:\n\n| FROM → TO | Best For | Key Adaptation |\n|-----------|----------|----------------|\n| ChatGPT → Claude | Long documents, deep analysis | Combine into single system prompt, use Projects |\n| Claude → ChatGPT | Plugins, GPTs for team | Split into two sections, create Custom GPT |\n| Any → Gemini | Google ecosystem, long context | System instructions + file uploads |\n| Any → Copilot | Microsoft 365 integration | Emphasize app-specific tasks |\n| Any → DeepSeek | Cost-effective high-volume | Single comprehensive system prompt |\n\n---\n\n## Common Migration Issues & Solutions\n\n### Issue: Response Style Differences\n**Symptom:** Platform responds differently than expected\n**Solution:** \n- Document the differences\n- Adjust language in instructions\n- Add explicit examples: \"Respond in this format: [example]\"\n\n### Issue: Lost Context\n**Symptom:** Migrated prompt missing key project details\n**Solution:**\n- Use file uploads (Claude Projects, Gemini)\n- Create knowledge documents\n- Break into modular components\n\n### Issue: Format Incompatibility\n**Symptom:** Prompt structure doesn't fit target platform\n**Solution:**\n- Reference migration templates above\n- Preserve core intent, adapt structure\n- Test with simple tasks first\n\n### Issue: Performance Differences\n**Symptom:** Tasks don't work as well on new platform\n**Solution:**\n- Adjust prompt specificity\n- Add examples of desired output\n- Iterate based on results\n- Consider platform strengths for different tasks\n\n---\n\n## Post-Migration Optimization\n\n### Week 1: Testing Phase\n- Test 5-10 typical tasks\n- Document response quality\n- Note any issues\n\n### Week 2: Refinement Phase\n- Adjust instructions based on testing\n- Add platform-specific optimizations\n- Create prompt library for common tasks\n\n### Week 3: Integration Phase\n- Incorporate into daily workflow\n- Train team members if applicable\n- Document best practices\n\n### Week 4: Evaluation Phase\n- Compare productivity to previous platform\n- Identify tasks better suited to old platform\n- Consider hybrid approach if needed\n\n---\n\n## Quick Migration Request Examples\n\nUser can say:\n- \"Migrate my ChatGPT custom instructions to Claude\"\n- \"Convert my Claude project setup for Gemini\"\n- \"Help me set up Copilot with my current AI preferences\"\n- \"Transfer my construction context to DeepSeek\"\n\nI will:\n1. Guide through export process\n2. Provide adapted content for target platform\n3. Include platform-specific tips\n4. Suggest testing approach",
      "limit": 100000,
