    {
      "value": "# Platform Knowledge\nComprehensive guide to major AI platforms for construction professionals.\n\n---\n\n## Platform Comparison Matrix\n\n| Platform | Best For | Context Window | Key Strength | Key Limitation |\n|----------|----------|----------------|--------------|----------------|\n| **ChatGPT (GPT-4o)** | General use, plugins, GPTs | 128K tokens | Ecosystem, plugins, Custom GPTs | Can be verbose, occasional hallucinations |\n| **Claude 3.5/4** | Long documents, analysis | 200K tokens | Nuanced reasoning, document analysis | No web browsing (Projects), slower |\n| **Gemini 1.5 Pro** | Google ecosystem, massive context | 1M+ tokens | Longest context, Google integration | Inconsistent quality, safety filters |\n| **Copilot** | Microsoft 365 integration | 128K tokens | Enterprise integration, web search | Enterprise-only features, variable quality |\n| **DeepSeek V3** | Cost-effective, technical tasks | 64K tokens | Very low cost, strong reasoning | Less polished, newer platform |\n\n---\n\n## ChatGPT (OpenAI)\n\n### Strengths\n- **Plugin ecosystem** — Access to PDF readers, web browsing, data analysis, image generation (DALL-E)\n- **Custom GPTs** — Create specialized assistants with knowledge files\n- **Memory feature** — Remembers user context across conversations\n- **Voice mode** — Mobile app supports voice conversations\n- **Data analysis** — Native Python execution for calculations, charts\n\n### Weaknesses\n- Can be overly verbose\n- May hallucinate specifics (codes, standards)\n- Custom instructions split into two sections (less intuitive)\n- Rate limits on free/Plus tiers\n\n### Best Use Cases for Construction\n- Drafting RFIs and correspondence (general)\n- Brainstorming solutions with web search\n- Creating custom GPTs for company templates\n- Quick document generation\n- Data analysis with spreadsheets\n\n### Pricing\n- **Free**: GPT-3.5 (limited GPT-4o access)\n- **Plus ($20/mo)**: GPT-4o, limited o1 access, custom GPTs\n- **Team ($25-30/user/mo)**: Shared GPTs, admin controls\n- **Enterprise**: Custom pricing, enhanced security\n\n### Recommended Setup\nUse Custom Instructions (two sections) + enable Memory feature. Consider creating a Custom GPT for project-specific work with uploaded templates and specs.\n\n---\n\n## Claude (Anthropic)\n\n### Strengths\n- **Extended thinking** — Shows reasoning process for complex analysis\n- **Exceptional writing quality** — Nuanced, professional tone\n- **Document analysis** — Upload PDFs, specs, contracts; reference specific sections\n- **Projects feature** — Knowledge files persist across conversations\n- **Large context window** — Handle entire spec books, contracts\n- **Safety/accuracy** — Lower hallucination rate, admits uncertainty\n\n### Weaknesses\n- No native web browsing in Projects mode\n- No plugins ecosystem\n- Slower response time for complex tasks\n- Artifacts can be clunky for some use cases\n\n### Best Use Cases for Construction\n- **Contract analysis** — Review entire contracts, highlight risks\n- **Spec review** — Compare submittals to uploaded specs\n- **RFI analysis** — Deep dive into complex conflicts\n- **Change order evaluation** — Thorough cost/schedule analysis\n- **Long document work** — Anything over 50 pages\n\n### Pricing\n- **Free**: Claude 3.5 Sonnet (limited messages)\n- **Pro ($20/mo)**: Higher limits, extended thinking, Projects\n- **Team ($25/user/mo)**: Shared projects, admin controls\n- **Enterprise**: Custom pricing, HIPAA compliance\n\n### Recommended Setup\nCreate a Claude Project with uploaded:\n- Company templates\n- Current project specs\n- Contract documents\n- Past RFI/CO examples for reference\n\n---\n\n## Google Gemini\n\n### Strengths\n- **Massive context** — 1M+ tokens (can process entire code bases, huge documents)\n- **Google integration** — Works with Google Docs, Sheets, Drive\n- **Native multimodal** — Images, video, audio, text in one\n- **Free tier is generous** — Good for budget-conscious users\n- **Web search** — Built-in, no plugin needed\n\n### Weaknesses\n- Inconsistent response quality\n- Heavy-handed safety filters (can block legitimate construction content)\n- Less polished than ChatGPT/Claude\n- Google account required\n\n### Best Use Cases for Construction\n- Working within Google Workspace ecosystem\n- Processing massive documents (full spec sets, codes)\n- Quick research with web search\n- Cost-sensitive projects\n- Collaborative Google Docs work\n\n### Pricing\n- **Free**: Gemini 1.5 Flash, limited Pro access\n- **Google One AI Premium ($20/mo)**: Gemini Advanced, 2TB storage\n- **Workspace add-on**: Enterprise integration\n\n### Recommended Setup\nUpload project documents to Google Drive and reference them directly. Use for work that's already in Google Workspace.\n\n---\n\n## Microsoft Copilot\n\n### Strengths\n- **Microsoft 365 integration** — Native Word, Excel, PowerPoint, Outlook\n- **Enterprise security** — Respects data boundaries, SOC2 compliant\n- **Web search** — Built-in with Bing\n- **Enterprise data access** — Can reference company documents (with permissions)\n- **Teams integration** — Meeting summaries, action items\n\n### Weaknesses\n- Quality can be inconsistent\n- Some features enterprise-only\n- Less flexible than standalone chatbots\n- Microsoft account/subscription required\n\n### Best Use Cases for Construction\n- Drafting documents directly in Word\n- Excel analysis and formulas\n- PowerPoint presentations for owners/meetings\n- Email drafting in Outlook\n- Teams meeting documentation\n- Enterprise environments with security requirements\n\n### Pricing\n- **Free**: Limited web-based access\n- **Copilot Pro ($20/mo)**: M365 integration, priority access\n- **Microsoft 365 Copilot ($30/user/mo)**: Full enterprise integration\n\n### Recommended Setup\nBest for organizations already using Microsoft 365. Enable for Word/Excel/PowerPoint workflows. Leverage for Teams meeting documentation.\n\n---\n\n## DeepSeek\n\n### Strengths\n- **Very low cost** — Fraction of competitors' pricing\n- **Strong reasoning** — Competitive with GPT-4 on many tasks\n- **Open source models available** — Can run locally for privacy\n- **Good for technical tasks** — Code, analysis, structured outputs\n\n### Weaknesses\n- Newer platform, less established\n- Smaller ecosystem (no plugins, GPTs)\n- Less polished UX\n- Support documentation limited\n\n### Best Use Cases for Construction\n- High-volume, cost-sensitive work\n- Technical analysis and calculations\n- Batch processing of documents\n- Teams with privacy requirements (self-hosted)\n\n### Pricing\n- **Free tier available**\n- **API pricing**: ~$0.14 per million input tokens (vs. ~$10 for GPT-4)\n- **Self-hosted**: Free (hardware costs only)\n\n### Recommended Setup\nGood for cost-conscious teams or those with technical expertise to self-host. Use for high-volume, routine prompt tasks.\n\n---\n\n## Platform Selection Guide\n\n### Choose ChatGPT When:\n- You want plugins (web browsing, PDF analysis, data visualization)\n- You need to create shareable custom GPTs for your team\n- You're doing mixed tasks (research, drafting, analysis)\n- You want voice conversations on mobile\n\n### Choose Claude When:\n- You're working with long documents (contracts, specs)\n- Quality of writing matters most\n- You need nuanced analysis of complex situations\n- You want extended thinking for thorough reasoning\n\n### Choose Gemini When:\n- You work in Google Workspace\n- You need the absolute longest context window\n- Budget is a primary concern\n- You need built-in web search\n\n### Choose Copilot When:\n- Your organization uses Microsoft 365\n- Enterprise security/compliance is required\n- You want AI integrated into Word, Excel, Outlook\n- You need Teams meeting documentation\n\n### Choose DeepSeek When:\n- Cost is the primary driver\n- You have high-volume, routine tasks\n- You have technical capability to self-host\n- You need privacy and can run locally\n\n---\n\n## Multi-Platform Strategy\n\nMany construction professionals benefit from using **multiple platforms**:\n\n| Platform | Use It For |\n|----------|------------|\n| **Claude** | Contract/spec review, complex analysis, important correspondence |\n| **ChatGPT** | Quick drafts, research, custom GPTs for repetitive tasks |\n| **Copilot** | M365 document creation, Teams meetings |\n| **Gemini** | Processing massive documents, Google Workspace work |\n\n---\n\n## Tips for Platform Hopping\n\n1. **Maintain consistent custom instructions** — Use my migration templates to transfer context\n2. **Store prompts centrally** — Use my prompt_library as your repository\n3. **Leverage each platform's strengths** — Don't force-fit a task to the wrong tool\n4. **Document what works** — Note which platform excels at which tasks for your workflow",
      "limit": 100000,
      "project_id": null,
      "template_name": null,
      "is_template": false,
      "template_id": null,
      "base_template_id": null,
      "deployment_id": null,
      "entity_id": null,
