      "value": "# Troubleshooting Guide\nCommon prompt problems, diagnosis, and fixes.\n\n---\n\n## How to Use This Guide\n\nWhen a prompt isn't producing the results you want:\n1. **Identify the symptom** — What's wrong with the output?\n2. **Find the matching issue below**\n3. **Apply the recommended fix**\n4. **Iterate as needed**\n\n---\n\n## Problem: Output Is Too Vague or Generic\n\n### Symptoms\n- Response could apply to any project\n- No specific numbers, names, or details\n- Feels like AI is hedging or avoiding specifics\n- \"It depends...\" or \"Consider...\" without clear direction\n\n### Likely Causes\n- Not enough context provided\n- AI wasn't given specific parameters\n- Task was too broad\n\n### Fixes\n\n**❌ Vague Prompt:**\n```\nWrite an RFI about the concrete issue.\n```\n\n**✅ Fixed Prompt:**\n```\nCONTEXT: $25M warehouse project, tilt-up concrete panel construction, \ncurrently installing panels on the north elevation. Panel #12 has a \nvisible crack at the door header opening, approximately 1/8\" wide and \n4' long. Structural engineer requested an RFI to document and get \ndesign direction.\n\nTASK: Draft an RFI to the structural engineer describing the condition \nand requesting repair/replacement guidance.\n\nFORMAT: Standard RFI format with RFI #, Date, Subject, Description, \nPhoto References, Impact Statement, and Question.\n```\n\n**Key additions:**\n- Project type and size\n- Specific condition details\n- Clear task and format\n\n---\n\n## Problem: AI Hallucinates Specifics\n\n### Symptoms\n- AI invents building codes, specifications, or standards\n- References documents that don't exist\n- Confident but wrong factual claims\n- Cites case law or legal precedents incorrectly\n\n### Likely Causes\n- Prompt asks AI to \"check code compliance\" without providing the code\n- Requesting specific references AI doesn't have access to\n- Asking for legal or engineering opinions beyond AI's scope\n\n### Fixes\n\n**❌ Hallucination-Prone Prompt:**\n```\nDoes this fire damper installation meet code requirements?\n```\n\n**✅ Safer Prompt:**\n```\nI'm reviewing a fire damper installation. The damper is installed in a \n2-hour fire-rated shaft wall penetration. The damper is a UL-listed \ncurtain-type fire damper, 24\" x 18\".\n\nPlease help me create a checklist of code requirements I should verify \nagainst the 2021 IBC and IMC. Include:\n- UL listing requirements\n- Installation per manufacturer's instructions\n- Access panel requirements\n- Damper actuator clearance\n- Testing and documentation requirements\n\nNote: I will verify these items against the actual code sections and \nmanufacturer's installation instructions. Do not cite specific code \nsection numbers unless you are certain.\n```\n\n**Key changes:**\n- AI helps create a checklist (appropriate task)\n- User verifies against actual codes (correct responsibility)\n- Explicit instruction not to invent code references\n\n---\n\n## Problem: Wrong Tone or Style\n\n### Symptoms\n- Too formal for internal communication\n- Too casual for owner/architect correspondence\n- Wrong audience (techs vs. executives)\n- Overly apologetic or defensive when should be direct\n\n### Likely Causes\n- No tone guidance in prompt\n- AI defaults to \"helpful assistant\" tone\n- Context didn't specify relationship or audience\n\n### Fixes\n\n**❌ No Tone Guidance:**\n```\nWrite an email to the owner about the delay.\n```\n\n**✅ With Tone Guidance:**\n```\nCONTEXT: We experienced a 3-day delay on the MEP rough-in due to \nunexpected existing conditions. The delay is within our float and \nwon't affect Substantial Completion.\n\nTASK: Draft an email to the owner's representative (Sarah Chen at \nABC Properties) notifying them of the delay.\n\nTONE: \n- Professional but direct\n- Confident (not apologetic — this was an unforeseen condition per contract)\n- Brief (Sarah prefers concise updates)\n- Forward-looking (focus on recovery plan, not just the problem)\n\nRELATIONSHIP: We have a good working relationship. This is a standard \nupdate, not a critical issue.\n```\n\n---\n\n## Problem: Output Structure Is Wrong\n\n### Symptoms\n- Wall of text instead of sections\n- No headers or organization\n- Missing requested elements\n- Format doesn't match your needs\n\n### Likely Causes\n- No format specified in prompt\n- Format request was too vague\n- AI didn't understand the desired structure\n\n### Fixes\n\n**❌ No Format Specified:**\n```\nReview this change order and tell me if it's fair.\n```\n\n**✅ Clear Format Request:**\n```\nReview the attached change order and provide your analysis.\n\nOUTPUT FORMAT:\nPlease structure your response exactly as follows:\n\n## Change Order Analysis\n\n### 1. Executive Summary\n[2-3 sentence overview of the CO and your assessment]\n\n### 2. Scope Verification\n| Item | Proposed Scope | Specs Reference | Assessment |\n|------|---------------|-----------------|------------|\n| [Table rows] |\n\n### 3. Pricing Analysis\n| Line Item | Proposed Cost | Fair Cost | Variance | Notes |\n|-----------|--------------|-----------|----------|-------|\n| [Table rows] |\n\n### 4. Red Flags\n- [Bullet list of concerns, if any]\n\n### 5. Recommendations\n[Your recommendation: Approve / Negotiate / Reject]\n\n### 6. Negotiation Talking Points\n[Numbered list of key discussion points]\n```\n\n**Key additions:**\n- Explicit section headers\n- Table format for data comparison\n- Numbered deliverables\n- Specific structure to follow\n\n---\n\n## Problem: AI Asks Too Many Clarifying Questions\n\n### Symptoms\n- Multiple back-and-forth exchanges needed\n- AI keeps saying \"I need more information\"\n- Simple tasks become lengthy conversations\n- Frustrating user experience\n\n### Likely Causes\n- Prompt missing key context\n- Overly broad task\n- AI being appropriately cautious but context wasn't provided upfront\n\n### Fixes\n\n**Prevention Strategy:** Use the CTF checklist before submitting:\n- [ ] Context: Project type, size, phase, relevant background\n- [ ] Task: Specific, well-defined action\n- [ ] Format: Desired output structure\n\n**❌ Incomplete Prompt:**\n```\nHelp me draft a submittal.\n```\n\n**✅ Complete Prompt (CTF):**\n```\nCONTEXT:\n- Project: $12M hospital renovation, currently in MEP rough-in phase\n- Submittal needed: Fire damper shop drawings\n- Spec section: 23 33 13 HVAC Dampers\n- Subcontractor: ABC Mechanical\n- Timeline: Need to review and return within 5 days\n\nTASK:\nCreate a transmittal letter to send the fire damper submittal to the \narchitect and mechanical engineer for review.\n\nFORMAT:\nStandard transmittal letter including:\n- Project name and number\n- Submittal number (assume #047)\n- Spec section reference\n- List of items being submitted (shop drawings, product data)\n- Distribution list\n- Request for review timeline confirmation\n```\n\n---\n\n## Problem: AI Doesn't Reference Attached Documents\n\n### Symptoms\n- Response ignores uploaded files\n- Generic response despite attached context\n- AI says \"I don't have access to that document\"\n\n### Likely Causes\n- Document not uploaded correctly (platform-specific)\n- AI not explicitly told to reference the attachment\n- File format not readable by the platform\n\n### Fixes\n\n**Step 1: Verify upload works on your platform**\n- **Claude**: Use Projects with knowledge files, or attach to conversation\n- **ChatGPT**: Attach files in conversation, or upload to Custom GPT\n- **Gemini**: Attach files or reference from Google Drive\n- **Copilot**: Attach files or reference from OneDrive/SharePoint\n\n**Step 2: Explicitly reference the attachment in your prompt**\n\n**❌ Implicit Reference:**\n```\nReview this RFI. [RFI attached]\n```\n\n**✅ Explicit Reference:**\n```\nAttached to this message is RFI #127 from the electrical subcontractor.\n\nPlease read the attached RFI and analyze it. In your response, \nreference specific details from the RFI text.\n\nTASK: Analyze the attached RFI #127 and provide:\n1. Summary of the issue\n2. Root cause assessment\n3. Three solution options\n4. Draft response\n\nReference specific details from the attached document in your analysis.\n```\n\n---\n\n## Problem: Output Is Too Long or Too Short\n\n### Symptoms\n- AI writes 2 pages when you need 2 paragraphs\n- AI gives one sentence when you need detailed analysis\n- Length doesn't match your needs\n\n### Likely Causes\n- No length guidance in prompt\n- AI defaults to verbose or brief based on task type\n- Format specification didn't include length constraints\n\n### Fixes\n\n**For Shorter Output:**\n```\n...Provide a BRIEF summary (2-3 sentences maximum).\nKeep your response concise. Do not elaborate on each point.\nExecutive summary format only.\n```\n\n**For Longer Output:**\n```\n...Provide a DETAILED analysis with comprehensive explanations.\nInclude examples and citations where appropriate.\nMinimum 500 words, fully developed sections.\n```\n\n**For Specific Length:**\n```\nYour response should be approximately 200-300 words.\nFormat as a one-page memo.\nKeep it to 3 short paragraphs.\n```\n\n---\n\n## Problem: AI Provides Incorrect Technical Information\n\n### Symptoms\n- Engineering or construction advice is wrong\n- AI misapplies codes or standards\n- Technical recommendations don't match real-world practice\n\n### Likely Causes\n- AI is a language model, not an engineer or code official\n- Prompt asks for expert-level technical judgment\n- Subject requires licensed professional input\n\n### Fixes\n\n**Prevention: Don't ask AI for:**\n- Structural engineering calculations\n- Code compliance certification\n- Safety-critical decisions\n- Legal interpretations\n- Professional engineering judgment\n\n**✅ Appropriate Use:**\n```\nHelp me draft an RFI to the structural engineer describing this \ncrack and requesting their assessment and repair recommendation.\n\nInclude in the RFI:\n- Clear description of the observed condition\n- Photos reference (I'll attach separately)\n- Request for repair method or replacement recommendation\n- Impact statement noting schedule sensitivity\n```\n\n**The AI helps draft the communication to the expert — it doesn't replace the expert.**\n\n---\n\n## Problem: Response Doesn't Match Platform Strengths\n\n### Symptoms\n- Using Claude for web research (it can't browse in Projects)\n- Using ChatGPT for massive document analysis (better in Gemini)\n- Platform limitations causing poor results\n\n### Likely Causes\n- Wrong platform selected for the task\n- Not leveraging platform-specific features\n\n### Fixes\n\n**Match task to platform:**\n\n| Task | Best Platform | Why |\n|------|---------------|-----|\n| Long document analysis | Claude | 200K context, excellent document handling |\n| Web research | ChatGPT, Gemini, Copilot | Native web browsing |\n| Massive context (full code books) | Gemini | 1M+ token context |\n| M365 document creation | Copilot | Native integration |\n| Cost-effective high volume | DeepSeek | Very low pricing |\n| Reusable assistant | ChatGPT Custom GPT | Shareable, configurable |\n\n**Ask me for platform recommendations:**\n- *\"Which platform should I use for analyzing this 100-page contract?\"*\n- *\"I need to create a custom AI assistant for my team — which platform?\"*\n\n---\n\n## Problem: AI Repeatedly Makes the Same Mistake\n\n### Symptoms\n- AI keeps including something you don't want\n- Corrections in one exchange don't persist\n- Each prompt requires re-stating preferences\n\n### Likely Causes\n- Preferences not saved to custom instructions or memory\n- Each conversation starts fresh\n- Feedback not captured in persistent context\n\n### Fixes\n\n**Option 1: Update Custom Instructions (ChatGPT, Claude, etc.)**\nAdd your preferences to your platform's custom instructions so they apply to all conversations.\n\n**Option 2: Ask me to save preferences**\n- *\"I always want you to use this format. Remember this.\"*\n- I'll update your user_preferences memory block\n\n**Option 3: Start with a preference reminder**\n```\nFor this and all future prompts in this conversation:\n- Use [specific format]\n- Avoid [specific thing you don't want]\n- Tone: [your preference]\n```\n\n---\n\n## Quick Troubleshooting Checklist\n\nWhen a prompt isn't working, check:\n\n- [ ] **Context** — Did I include project type, size, phase?\n- [ ] **Task** — Is my request specific and actionable?\n- [ ] **Format** — Did I specify the output structure?\n- [ ] **Tone** — Did I indicate the appropriate voice?\n- [ ] **Length** — Is my length expectation clear?\n- [ ] **Attachments** — Did I explicitly reference uploaded files?\n- [ ] **Platform** — Am I using the right AI for this task?\n- [ ] **Scope** — Am I asking for something AI can't/shouldn't do?\n\n---\n\n## Common Error Messages & Solutions\n\n### \"I don't have access to that information\"\n- **Cause**: File not uploaded or referenced correctly\n- **Fix**: Explicitly reference attachments; verify upload succeeded\n\n### \"I'm not able to browse the web\"\n- **Cause**: Using Claude Projects or platform without web access\n- **Fix**: Switch to ChatGPT/Gemini/Copilot for web research, or provide the information in your prompt\n\n### \"I can't verify that information\"\n- **Cause**: AI correctly noting it can't confirm specifics\n- **Fix**: This is appropriate behavior. Verify critical information yourself.\n\n### \"This requires professional judgment\"\n- **Cause**: AI correctly deferring to expert\n- **Fix**: This is appropriate. Use AI to draft communication to experts.\n\n---\n\n## Getting Help\n\nIf you can't resolve a prompt issue:\n\n1. **Say**: *\"This prompt isn't working the way I want. Can you help me improve it?\"*\n2. **Share**: The prompt you tried and what went wrong\n3. **I'll diagnose**: Identify the issue and suggest a fix\n4. **We iterate**: Refine until it works\n\nRemember: Good prompting is iterative. It's normal to refine prompts as you learn what works.",
      "limit": 100000,
      "project_id": null,
      "template_name": null,
      "is_template": false,
      "template_id": null,
      "base_template_id": null,
